From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000008 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tab S9 FE Linux Project <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 13:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ANDROID: bringup: omit crash injector and initialize charger event

sec_debug_test is a deliberate crash/corruption injection facility, not a
driver needed by Linux userspace.  It also embeds FPSIMD instructions in a
kernel built with -mgeneral-regs-only.  Do not include it in the bring-up
kernel.

Initialize the SM5714 notification value.  The receiving battery callback only
uses this property as an event, but passing indeterminate data is still invalid
C and is rejected by modern Clang.

Signed-off-by: Tab S9 FE Linux Project <noreply@example.invalid>
---
 drivers/battery/charger/sm5714_charger/sm5714_charger.c | 2 +-
 drivers/samsung/debug/Makefile                           | 1 -
 2 files changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/battery/charger/sm5714_charger/sm5714_charger.c b/drivers/battery/charger/sm5714_charger/sm5714_charger.c
--- a/drivers/battery/charger/sm5714_charger/sm5714_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/battery/charger/sm5714_charger/sm5714_charger.c
@@ -1292,7 +1292,7 @@ static inline int _reduce_input_limit_current(struct sm5714_charger_data *charger
 
 static inline void _check_slow_rate_charging(struct sm5714_charger_data *charger)
 {
-	union power_supply_propval value;
+	union power_supply_propval value = { 0 };
 
 	if (charger->input_current <= SLOW_CHARGING_CURRENT_STANDARD &&
 			charger->cable_type != SEC_BATTERY_CABLE_NONE) {
diff --git a/drivers/samsung/debug/Makefile b/drivers/samsung/debug/Makefile
--- a/drivers/samsung/debug/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/samsung/debug/Makefile
@@ -7,6 +7,5 @@ sec_debug-y				+= sec_debug_base.o
 sec_debug-y				+= sec_dump_sink.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SEC_DEBUG_BASE)		+= sec_debug_base_early.o
-obj-$(CONFIG_SEC_DEBUG_BASE)		+= sec_debug_test.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SEC_DEBUG_BASE)		+= sec_debug_dprm.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SEC_DEBUG_BASE)		+= sec_debug_dprt.o
 
-- 
